&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Given:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The total salary of A and B is Rs. 20000&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A spends 50% and B spends 75% of their salary respectively&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The ratio of their savings is 3 : 1&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calculation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let, the salary of A is = X, and the salary of B = (20000 - X)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Saving of A = X(100 - 50)/100 = 50X/100&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Saving of B = (20000 - X)&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; (100 - 75)/100 = 25(20000 - X)/100&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;According to the question,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; (50X/100) / (&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;25(20000 - X)/100) = 3/1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr; 50X = 3&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; (500000 - 25X)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr; 125X = 1500000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr; X = 12000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The salary of B = 20000 - 12000 = Rs. 8000&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The annual salary of B = 12&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 8000 = Rs. 96000&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;there4; The correct answer is option 5&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

