&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bolder;&quot;&gt;Calculation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Calculate investment months (capital &amp;times; time)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A: 12000 &amp;times; 12 = 144000&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;B: 16000 &amp;times; 8 = 128000&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Total = 144000 + 128000 = 272000&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Profit Ratio of A:B = 144000:128000 = 9 : 8&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Share of profit of B is Rs. 4800&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So, 8 unit = 4800&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So, 9 unit &amp;nbsp;= 4800 &amp;times; 9 / 8 =5400&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So, A&amp;rsquo;s share of profit is Rs. 5400&lt;/p&gt;

